  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $\\theta\\in[-\\pi,\\pi]$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin(2\\theta)=\\frac{1}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=-\\frac{11\\pi}{12},-\\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\frac{\\pi}{12},\\frac{5\\pi}{12}$.\n\nSolve for $2\\theta$ on $[-2\\pi,2\\pi]$, then divide by $2$.",
          "worked": "Let $u=2\\theta$, so $u\\in[-2\\pi,2\\pi]$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin u&=\\frac{1}{2}\\\\u&=-\\frac{11\\pi}{6},\\ -\\frac{7\\pi}{6},\\ \\frac{\\pi}{6},\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{u}{2}\\\\\\theta&=-\\frac{11\\pi}{12},\\ -\\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\ \\frac{\\pi}{12},\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos(2\\theta)=-\\frac{1}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\pm\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pm\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$.\n\nSolve for $2\\theta$ on $[-2\\pi,2\\pi]$, then divide by $2$.",
          "worked": "Let $u=2\\theta$, so $u\\in[-2\\pi,2\\pi]$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos u&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\\\u&=-\\frac{4\\pi}{3},\\ -\\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{u}{2}\\\\\\theta&=\\pm\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\ \\pm\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$.",
          "worked": "Let $u=\\frac{\\theta}{2}$, so $u\\in\\left[-\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin u&=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\u&=-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=2u\\\\\\theta&=-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\left(\\theta-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\right)=\\sqrt3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=-\\pi,0,\\pi$.\n\nTransform the interval for $\\theta-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$ and retain both endpoints after back-substitution.",
          "worked": "Let $u=\\theta-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$, so $u\\in\\left[-\\frac{5\\pi}{3},\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right]$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan u&=\\sqrt3\\\\u&=-\\frac{5\\pi}{3},\\ -\\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=u+\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=-\\pi,\\ 0,\\ \\pi\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
